<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2022-tame-02--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2022-tame-02: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.51";
    dc:description "Memory here has a workable behavioral meaning: faster return to criterion after training, measured again after the head regenerates. Published tables from the automated familiarization study and older training papers contain summary counts, scattered across journals rather than in one archive. Those summaries can be re-read for effect direction, and they leave the main confounds and the raw latencies unchecked.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Compare time-to-criterion or savings after regeneration between animals trained before decapitation and naive regenerates; persistence holds if trained animals relearn faster after a new brain is built, with motility equated.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Classical manual studies and the 2013 familiarization assay do not cover the same tasks.", "Raw tracking logs from the automated assay were not deposited.", "Residual body tissue, sensitization, and one-tailed tests can mimic savings without a memory stored outside the original brain.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.7"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.513"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2022-tame-02--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2022-tame-02 by Grok 4.7: 0.45";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
